# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
*.spec.bak

# ── Installer output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
installer/JobFinder-Setup*.exe
installer/JobFinder*.dmg

# ── PyInstaller ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python

# ── User data (never commit) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/
logs/
data/jobfinder.db
data/resume_profile.json
data/widget_pos.json

# ── Resume (personal file) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.pdf
*.docx

# ── API keys / secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# config.yaml holds the real local config (incl. secrets) and is never committed.
# config.example.yaml is the committed template — keep every credential field
# in it blank. If you accidentally commit a key, rotate it immediately at
# console.anthropic.com

# ── Python virtual environments ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env

# ── IDEs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.suo
*.user

# ── OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
config.yaml
*.yaml
!config.example.yaml
!.pre-commit-config.yaml
# Test fixture configs (T53). The blanket `*.yaml` above exists to keep a
# real config.yaml — which holds live credentials — out of the repo, and
# that still holds everywhere else. These are committed on purpose: a
# round-trip test that proves "a config the old build wrote still loads
# with every value preserved" is only worth anything if the config it
# loads is a frozen artifact in version control rather than something the
# test generates from today's code. Credential-shaped values under this
# path must stay obviously fake.
!tests/fixtures/config/*.yaml
browsers/
data/user_extras.yaml

# ── Local tool and editor state (never commit) ────────────────────────────────
# Machine-local scratch belonging to whoever is working in the tree, not to the
# project. These can appear in any subdirectory a tool is run from, so each
# pattern is anchored both at the root and recursively.
.claude/
**/.claude/
.harness-worktrees/
.harness/
